                || String(post.graphic_deliverable_id || '').trim());
        }
        if (comp === 'video') {
            return !!(String(post.linear_issue_id || '').trim()
                || String(post.video_deliverable_id || '').trim());
        }
        return true;
    }
    /* WHAT A COMPONENT PILL SHOULD DISPLAY (owner ruling 2026-08-20).
       A video/graphic slot with no Linear sub-issue has no work item behind
       it, so "In Progress" is a claim the card cannot support. The SMM card
       already greys and disables such a pill; the client had no signal at all.
       Both now read N/A.

       ONE helper for four render paths -- the calendar card, the samples card
       and both in-place pill updaters -- because they drift otherwise: an
       in-place update that recomputed the label from the stored status would
       quietly put "In Progress" back on a pill the full render had shown as
       N/A.

       DISPLAY ONLY. Callers keep the STORED status in `data-val` and in every
       write path. The owner ruled on 2026-08-19 that N/A is a manual SMM
       choice the system must never write, and the reconcilers park a card
       whose STORED status is N/A, so a write here would change reconciliation
       behaviour too.

       A finished state is never masked: Approved / Scheduled / Posted are the
       states the client is entitled to see, and one must not vanish behind
